  "body": "## Result\n\nThis PR completes the explicit open billing question from [PR #1782](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/1782): the fixed seed-42, 205-pair helper-sharing wrapper on the pinned selected R439 word is now a complete local ADD-gate construction with an exact invoice.\n\n- Complete ADDs: **24,305 \u2192 18,074**, net saving **6,231**. All 410 helper preparation/restoration ADD gates are charged.\n- D source ADDs: 18,085 \u2192 11,854; D gates: 111 \u2192 521.\n- The 661-column dirty-input map, forward and reverse, is unchanged. Semantic N equals raw K, the D cut state/frame paths and paid profile remain identical (rank mass 5,129).\n- Exact envelopes: F 49,347 \u2192 75,381; B 1,113,070 \u2192 1,196,402. The local and nine-stage bills are 95/104 and 180/192 bits. The literal recurrence and official record exporter agree.\n\nThis is one local R439 word construction. The seed-42 matching is inherited and not claimed optimal. The selected bit side remains nonbinding; no selected-supplier adoption, outer assembly, or \u03ba change is claimed. The inherited gate-local H2/K flags remain false; the construction uses the scoped PR1194/PR1782 semantic H2/K contract.\n\n## Reproduce\n\n```sh\npython3 -I -B research/r439-copyshare-priced-wrap-seedaaa3e40/verify.py\npython3 scripts/research_package.py --package research/r439-copyshare-priced-wrap-seedaaa3e40 --check-only\n```\n\nBoth commands pass locally under CPython 3.14.7. The registered package runner requires Python 3.12, which is unavailable in this environment; the hosted workflow should provide that replay. The verifier includes source pins, the full invoice, positive controls, and five negative controls.\n\n## Pins and overlap\n\n- Base: `0fdd7d82de03e43c9e5a1000dfbcd380d1b687d2` (refreshed immediately before submission; canonical `main` is unchanged).\n- Selected-record SHA-256: `10b9e340fd8e354a37a0c4813c90e5de1dd42044b5f6aca4a3fc5a42b685fa32`.\n- Priority revision 4; seed `aaa3e40dfc71629ff8180ede0cda4c96`; task `bit-helper-contract`; catalogue SHA-256 `d46eb6d5b3e279428753d770653663fbdf1063e55c255ea073d768f344927ef7`.\n- The final complete overlap cache covered 435 open PRs and 877 Discussion records (23:03\u201323:05Z). A direct live open-PR search found no same-word priced construction. PR #2033's fixed pair is on the distinct PR1062 star-composed word and is not evidence for this candidate.\n- Claim and result extend the PR1782 handoff in [Discussion #1166](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/discussions/1166#discussioncomment-18935773).\n\nPrepared by Cinna Davis with substantial OpenAI Codex assistance in scoping, construction, exact invoice verification and packaging. Predecessor attribution and Apache-2.0 license are included in the package.\n",
